{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' research_journal.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Forecasting research journal\n\n## Best and protocol\nResumed 2026-10-06 14:08 UTC. Retained best in **`method.py`**: graph-seasonal network + graph-regularized **sensor/disagreement expert gate**, complete masked MAE **13.978237919663384**, score **3.0498715778981134**, evaluation `15f14f3f1c39446d8fc12dcbd78034f2`. Improves sensor/horizon **13.992852028244142** by **0.014614108580758**, and unchanged turn-start **14.005432390047323** by **0.027194470383939**. Backup entry point `/tmp/forecast_turn_graph/method.site_context_best`. Required final complete best-method verification is running; record its response before ending.\n\nEvery public result below is an actual `./solve.sh` response with unchanged complete seeds **17, 29, 43**, fresh fits and independent reloads. Successful runs passed all quality gates. Only public calibration targets and features accessed; no development labels, held-out/reference data, other track or target reconstruction from histories. No downloads or frozen/scorer edits. All frozen SHA-256 checks passed. At most two CPU threads; 16 source files, well within source/state limits.\n\nFirst action this turn was unchanged public scoring. Initial call and two spaced retries returned HTTP 409 while prior-turn evaluation was busy; accepted 14:15 run then passed. No MAE was inferred from failed requests.\n\n## Runnable method\nPooled median residual tree and horizon 1-6 / 7-12 specialists, equally blended: 90 stages, 15 leaves, minimum leaf 250, L2 20. Inputs include base/anchor/history summaries, forecast slopes, clock/horizon, sensor ID, eight neighbors learned from within-history change correlations, scale-normalized context.\n\nNumPy residual network: 6D sensor embeddings, 48/24 tanh layers, linear skip, two daily Fourier harmonics, smooth absolute loss (2 traffic units), 100 Adam epochs/batch 4096. Sensor intercept/horizon/four-periodic head: L2 0.0005; symmetric learned-neighbor Laplacian 0.005 on periodic coefficients only.\n\nThree contiguous calibration-origin cross-fits supply held-out tree/network predictions for a sigmoid gate. Global inputs: horizon, relative anchor/base and recent/base disagreement, history variability, expert disagreement, flow; four centered-horizon interactions. Coefficient L2 0.01 toward the 0.18 short / 0.32 long network schedule; weights clipped [0.05, 0.65]. Sensor gate coefficients are centered across sensors and penalized by mean ridge 0.02 plus learned-neighbor Laplacian 0.05. Sensor/horizon has two coefficients; sensor/context adds two normalized disagreement slopes. No extra backbone fits are needed for the node gate.\n\n## Complete public results\n| Method | Masked MAE | Decision |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Initial identity | 15.4218571566 | Baseline |\n| Robust pooled/sensor linear | 15.0648913575 | Superseded |\n| Median tree, 90 stages | 14.1452638897 | Superseded; exact repeats |\n| Tree, 180 stages | 14.1455193190 | Rejected |\n| Learned-neighborhood tree | 14.1214289791 | Superseded |\n| Neighbor tree + sensor affine | 14.1433545829 | Rejected despite local gain |\n| Anchor-aligned seasonal innovations | 14.1209047365 | Superseded |\n| Partially pooled horizon trees | 14.1101708074 | Superseded |\n| Trees + 25% smooth network | 14.0354537227 | Superseded |\n| Quarter-strength cross-fitted neural correction | 14.0429518732 | Rejected despite local gain |\n| Horizon-scheduled 18%/32% network | 14.030202610462462 | Superseded |\n| Unheaded network + gate | 14.018026311821254 | Superseded; exact repeat |\n| Gated summary/relative-history ensemble | 14.031298204247088 | Rejected |\n| Matching gate + independent seasonal head | 14.020179462432948 | Rejected |\n| Graph-seasonal head + standard gate | 14.007650660881973 | Superseded; `f97eaab0c1764a1095465feadf1ed8ef` |\n| Graph head + horizon interactions (unchanged turn start) | 14.005432390047323 | Superseded; `781ee1eee85948349c5d6019155a6ba3` |\n| Graph head + sensor/horizon gate | 13.992852028244142 | Superseded; `c64f72f831ca4f5cb218298f8842401a` |\n| Graph head + sensor/disagreement gate | **13.978237919663384** | Retained; `15f14f3f1c39446d8fc12dcbd78034f2` |\n\n## This-turn calibration experiments\nCalibration: 74 hourly origins, 12 horizons, 170 sensors. All local comparisons seed 17: train 0:50/test 50:74 (last), train 0:25 plus 49:74/test 25:49 (middle). Matching inner OOF excludes held origins. Local MAE is diagnostic, never the protected metric. Own caches/scripts: `/tmp/forecast_turn_graph/`; avoid scorer-owned temporary directories.\n\n| Implemented method / control | Last MAE | Middle MAE | Decision |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Graph/standard gate | 13.4326290 | 13.1833977 | Earlier best |\n| Graph/horizon interactions | 13.4303059279 | 13.1785833588 | Turn-start control |\n| Innovation sensor head (3 bounded relative slopes) | 13.4402536270 | 13.1793631069 | Rejected |\n| Graph embedding regularization (0.002) | 13.4635236623 | 13.2025820717 | Rejected |\n| Four periodic global gate inputs | 13.4880380418 | 13.1805876745 | Rejected |\n| Sensor intercept gate | 13.4251230631 | 13.1595806816 | Superseded locally |\n| Sensor intercept/horizon gate | 13.4250415890 | 13.1573790747 | Public improvement |\n| Interaction gate + learned correction amplitude | 13.4587914185 | 13.1927627363 | Rejected |\n| Sensor/horizon + correction amplitude | 13.4410828461 | 13.1710047981 | Rejected |\n| Sensor/disagreement gate (`site_context`) | 13.3974505397 | 13.1268084431 | Public improvement; retained |\n| Five origin-bootstrap context gates, averaged | 13.4040037221 | 13.1377383632 | Rejected |\n| Context + shared signed inputs (`site_context_signed`) | 13.4021680050 | 13.1247723040 | Mixed; defer |\n| Context + shared/sensor signed slopes (`site_direction`) | 13.3957087626 | 13.1253872203 | Next public discriminator |\n\nAmplitude used 0.5-1.5 tanh factor, smooth MAE and coefficient ridge 0.02. Directional extension has two extra signed relative features globally plus their node-specific slopes; shared-only control keeps four node terms, full directional has six. Existing feature bounds remain.\n\nFive bootstrap context refits remained better than sensor/horizon: last 13.39090-13.42223, middle 13.13098-13.15157, but averaging worsened full-fit context. Feature-only development context-weight checks were finite, upper-cap fractions 0.208% / 0.537%, lower below 0.01%. Sensor/horizon gains are heterogeneous: 76/170 sensors improve last, 98/170 middle; nodes 54/60/144 benefit most on both blocks. Gate pickle reload reproduced weights exactly.\n\n## Earlier failures and lessons\nDo not repeat unchanged experiments: tree history lags/sensor profiles, robust summaries, heteroscedastic tree scaling, neighbor seasonal innovations, three horizon groups, origin bootstrap trees, physical-graph replacement/augmentation, short-training network, chronological/relative-history network replacement, epoch-75-99 parameter averaging, directional expert-distance agreement gates. Rich history inputs lowered training MAE but worsened pure validation; their ensemble and independent seasonal heads also failed public scoring despite paired local gains. Graph sharing of periodic coefficients transferred better.\n\nPublic feature-only check: development anchor/base disagreement tail is heavier (99th percentile 1.492 vs calibration 0.583); keep relative variables bounded. Local gains are not proof of public improvement.\n\n## Next action\nRecord final complete verification response. Next turn: read this journal and run unchanged retained method first, then test `gate_mode='site_direction'` with matching graph head under complete seeds, comparing against **13.978237919663384**. It has small paired local gains but no public result. If rejected, investigate four network-wide context summaries in the existing network module, keeping summary inputs rather than full history expansion. Shared-only signed control had mixed local results; bootstrap gate averaging was worse on both blocks, so prefer the full directional candidate before repeating those controls.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' method.py && printf '\\\\n--- solve.sh ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,120p' solve.sh && printf '\\\\n--- notes ---\\\\n' && cat method_notes.json\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Graph-shared seasonal experts with sensor-conditional reliability logits.\"\"\"\nimport conditional_calibration\n\n\ndef fit(features, targets, seed):\n    return conditional_calibration.fit(features, targets, seed, site_head='graph',\n                                       gate_mode='site_context')\n\n\ndef predict(state, features):\n    return conditional_calibration.predict(state, features)\n\n--- solve.sh ---\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\npython /opt/forecast-engine/evaluate.py --solution /workspace/solution\n\n--- notes ---\n{\n  \"policy_name\": \"graph_regularized_sensor_context_blend\",\n  \"method_summary\": \"Adds sensor-specific intercepts, horizon slopes and bounded anchor/history-disagreement slopes to cross-fitted logits blending median residual trees with a graph-seasonal residual network, using ridge and learned-neighbor Laplacian penalties. Complete protected masked MAE improves from 14.0054323900 to 13.9782379197 under unchanged seeds 17, 29 and 43, with all quality gates passing; the sensor-context method is retained.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"for f in calibration.py conditional_calibration.py neural_calibration.py stacked_calibration.py; do printf '\\\\n--- %s ---\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"\n--- calibration.py ---\n\"\"\"Robust hierarchical residual calibration of fixed traffic forecasts.\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom threadpoolctl import threadpool_limits\n\n\ndef _design(features):\n    b = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float64)\n    a = np.asarray(features['anchor'], dtype=np.float64)\n    hist = np.asarray(features['history'], dtype=np.float64)\n    clock = np.asarray(features['clock'], dtype=np.float64)\n    hh = np.broadcast_to(np.linspace(-1.0, 1.0, b.shape[1])[None, :, None], b.shape)\n    recent = np.broadcast_to(np.median(hist[:, -3:, :], axis=1)[:, None, :], b.shape)\n    older = np.broadcast_to(np.median(hist[:, :6, :], axis=1)[:, None, :], b.shape)\n    allmean = np.broadcast_to(np.mean(hist, axis=1)[:, None, :], b.shape)\n    sine = np.sin(2 * np.pi * clock)\n    cosine = np.cos(2 * np.pi * clock)\n    anchor = np.clip((a - b) / 50, -5, 5)\n    level = b / 300\n    recent_delta = np.clip((recent - b) / 50, -5, 5)\n    trend = np.clip((recent - older) / 50, -5, 5)\n    arr = [np.ones_like(b), hh, hh * hh, sine, cosine,\n           np.sin(4 * np.pi * clock), np.cos(4 * np.pi * clock),\n           level, anchor, anchor * hh, recent_delta, recent_delta * hh,\n           np.clip((allmean - b) / 50, -5, 5), trend, trend * hh,\n           sine * hh, cosine * hh, sine * level, cosine * level]\n    return np.stack(arr, axis=-1)\n\n\ndef _global_fit(x, y, valid, iterations=8):\n    xx = x.reshape(-1, x.shape[-1])\n    yy = y.reshape(-1)\n    ok = valid.reshape(-1)\n    xx = xx[ok]\n    yy = yy[ok]\n    coef = np.zeros(xx.shape[1])\n    penalty = np.eye(xx.shape[1]) * 2.0\n    for _ in range(iterations):\n        residual = yy - xx @ coef\n        w = 1.0 / np.maximum(np.abs(residual), 4.0)\n        coef = np.linalg.solve(xx.T @ (w[:, None] * xx) + penalty,\n                               xx.T @ (w * yy))\n    return coef\n\n\ndef fit(features, targets, seed):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        x = _design(features)\n        y = np.asarray(targets['target'] if isinstance(targets, dict) else targets,\n                       dtype=np.float64)\n        base = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float64)\n        valid = np.isfinite(y) & (y > 0)\n        y = np.where(valid, y - base, 0)\n        global_coef = _global_fit(x, y, valid)\n        # Every sensor gets a regularized deviation from the pooled model.\n        xx = x.transpose(2, 0, 1, 3).reshape(x.shape[2], -1, x.shape[-1])\n        yy = y.transpose(2, 0, 1).reshape(x.shape[2], -1)\n        mask = valid.transpose(2, 0, 1).reshape(x.shape[2], -1)\n        prior = np.broadcast_to(global_coef, (x.shape[2], x.shape[-1])).copy()\n        coef = prior.copy()\n        strength = np.array([3, 20, 40, 15, 15, 30, 30,\n                             60, 40, 80, 60, 100, 60, 80, 100,\n                             50, 50, 60, 60], dtype=np.float64)\n        reg = np.diag(strength)\n        for _ in range(8):\n            residual = yy - np.einsum('nrp,np->nr', xx, coef)\n            w = mask / np.maximum(np.abs(residual), 4.0)\n            gram = np.einsum('nrp,nr,nrq->npq', xx, w, xx, optimize=True)\n            rhs = np.einsum('nrp,nr,nr->np', xx, w, yy, optimize=True)\n            coef = np.linalg.solve(gram + reg, (rhs + prior * strength)[..., None])[..., 0]\n        return {'version': 2, 'coef': coef.astype(np.float32)}\n\n\ndef predict(state, features):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        x = _design(features)\n        correction = np.einsum('shnp,np->shn', x, np.asarray(state['coef']))\n        return np.maximum(np.asarray(features['base']) + correction, 0).astype(np.float32)\n\n--- conditional_calibration.py ---\n\"\"\"Cross-fitted, regularized conditional blending of residual experts.\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom scipy.special import expit\nfrom threadpoolctl import threadpool_limits\nimport blended_calibration\nimport horizon_calibration\nimport neural_calibration\nimport spatial_calibration\n\n\ndef _design(features, tree, network, mode='standard'):\n    base = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float64)\n    anchor = np.asarray(features['anchor'], dtype=np.float64)\n    history = np.asarray(features['history'], dtype=np.float64)\n    scale = np.maximum(np.mean(history, axis=1)[:, None, :], 30)\n    recent = np.mean(history[:, -3:, :], axis=1)[:, None, :]\n    std = np.std(history, axis=1)[:, None, :]\n    horizon = np.broadcast_to(np.arange(base.shape[1])[None, :, None] / 11, base.shape)\n    def broadcast(v):\n        return np.broadcast_to(v, base.shape)\n    variables = [np.ones_like(base), horizon,\n                 np.clip(np.abs(anchor - base) / scale, 0, 2),\n                 np.clip(np.abs(recent - base) / scale, 0, 2),\n                 broadcast(np.clip(std / scale, 0, 2)),\n                 np.clip(np.abs(network - tree) / 20, 0, 3),\n                 np.clip(base / 200, 0, 3)]\n    if mode == 'agreement':\n        last = history[:, -1:, :]\n        for reference in (anchor, recent, last):\n            variables.append(np.clip((np.abs(tree - reference) -\n                                      np.abs(network - reference)) / 20, -3, 3))\n    if mode in ('interactions', 'site', 'site_horizon', 'site_context', 'site_direction',\n                'site_context_signed', 'periodic'):\n        variables.extend([(horizon - 0.5) * variables[j] for j in (2, 3, 4, 5)])\n    if mode in ('site_direction', 'site_context_signed'):\n        variables.extend([np.clip((anchor - base) / scale, -2, 2),\n                          np.clip((recent - base) / scale, -2, 2)])\n    if mode == 'periodic':\n        clock = np.asarray(features['clock'], dtype=np.float64)\n        variables.extend([np.sin(2 * np.pi * clock), np.cos(2 * np.pi * clock),\n                          np.sin(4 * np.pi * clock), np.cos(4 * np.pi * clock)])\n    return np.stack(variables, axis=-1).reshape(-1, len(variables))\n\n\ndef _gate_fit(features, target, tree, network, penalty=0.01, mode='standard'):\n    x = _design(features, tree, network, mode)\n    valid = (np.isfinite(target) & (target > 0)).reshape(-1)\n    x = x[valid]\n    center = x.mean(axis=0)\n    center[0] = 0\n    scale = np.maximum(x.std(axis=0), 0.1)\n    scale[0] = 1\n    x = np.clip((x - center) / scale, -4, 4)\n    residual = (tree - target).reshape(-1)[valid]\n    difference = (network - tree).reshape(-1)[valid]\n    weight0 = np.broadcast_to(np.where(np.arange(tree.shape[1]) < 6, 0.18, 0.32)[None, :, None], tree.shape).reshape(-1)[valid]\n    offset = np.log(weight0 / (1 - weight0))\n    use_site = mode in ('site', 'site_horizon', 'site_context', 'site_direction', 'site_context_signed')\n    if use_site:\n        nodes = tree.shape[2]\n        node = np.broadcast_to(np.arange(nodes)[None, None, :], tree.shape).reshape(-1)[valid]\n        width = {'site': 1, 'site_horizon': 2, 'site_context': 4, 'site_direction': 6,\n                 'site_context_signed': 4}[mode]\n        basis = np.ones((len(node), width))\n        if width >= 2:\n            basis[:, 1] = np.broadcast_to(np.linspace(-1, 1, tree.shape[1])[None, :, None], tree.shape).reshape(-1)[valid]\n        site_columns = [2, 3] if width >= 4 else []\n        if width == 6:\n            site_columns.extend([11, 12])\n        if site_columns:\n            basis[:, 2:] = x[:, site_columns]\n        graph = spatial_calibration._neighborhood(features)\n        adjacency = np.zeros((nodes, nodes))\n        np.put_along_axis(adjacency, graph['neighbors'], graph['weights'], axis=1)\n        adjacency = (adjacency + adjacency.T) / 2\n        laplacian = np.diag(adjacency.sum(axis=1)) - adjacency\n        site_shape = (nodes, basis.shape[1])\n    def objective(coef):\n        global_coef = coef[:x.shape[1]]\n        logit = offset + x @ global_coef\n        if use_site:\n            site = coef[x.shape[1]:].reshape(site_shape)\n            centered_site = site - site.mean(axis=0)\n            logit += np.sum(centered_site[node] * basis, axis=1)\n        weight = expit(logit)\n        error = residual + weight * difference\n        smooth = np.sqrt(error * error + 4)\n        derivative = error / smooth * difference * weight * (1 - weight)\n        value = np.mean(smooth) / 20 + penalty * np.dot(global_coef, global_coef) / 2\n        gradient = x.T @ derivative / (len(x) * 20) + penalty * global_coef\n        if use_site:\n            site_gradient = np.column_stack([\n                np.bincount(node, weights=derivative * basis[:, j], minlength=nodes)\n                for j in range(basis.shape[1])]) / (len(x) * 20)\n            site_gradient -= site_gradient.mean(axis=0)\n            regularizer = 0.02 * site + 0.05 * (laplacian @ site)\n            site_gradient += regularizer / nodes\n            value += np.sum(site * regularizer) / (2 * nodes)\n            gradient = np.r_[gradient, site_gradient.reshape(-1)]\n        return value, gradient\n    count = x.shape[1] + nodes * basis.shape[1] if use_site else x.shape[1]\n    result = minimize(objective, np.zeros(count), jac=True, method='L-BFGS-B',\n                      options={'maxiter': 100 if use_site else 60, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    state = {'coef': result.x[:x.shape[1]].astype(np.float32), 'center': center.astype(np.float32),\n             'scale': scale.astype(np.float32), 'penalty': penalty, 'mode': mode}\n    if use_site:\n        site = result.x[x.shape[1]:].reshape(site_shape)\n        state['site'] = (site - site.mean(axis=0)).astype(np.float32)\n        state['site_columns'] = site_columns\n    return state\n\n\ndef _weight(state, features, tree, network):\n    x = _design(features, tree, network, state.get('mode', 'standard'))\n    x = np.clip((x - state['center']) / state['scale'], -4, 4)\n    initial = np.broadcast_to(np.where(np.arange(tree.shape[1]) < 6, 0.18, 0.32)[None, :, None], tree.shape)\n    offset = np.log(initial / (1 - initial))\n    logit = offset + (x @ state['coef']).reshape(tree.shape)\n    if 'site' in state:\n        site = state['site']\n        logit += site[None, None, :, 0]\n        if site.shape[1] >= 2:\n            logit += np.linspace(-1, 1, tree.shape[1])[None, :, None] * site[None, None, :, 1]\n        for j, column in enumerate(state.get('site_columns', range(2, site.shape[1])), 2):\n            logit += x[:, column].reshape(tree.shape) * site[None, None, :, j]\n    return np.clip(expit(logit), 0.05, 0.65)\n\n\ndef _amplitude_design(features, correction):\n    base = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float64)\n    history = np.asarray(features['history'], dtype=np.float64)\n    scale = np.maximum(np.mean(history, axis=1)[:, None, :], 30)\n    anchor = np.asarray(features['anchor'])\n    recent = np.mean(history[:, -3:, :], axis=1)[:, None, :]\n    horizon = np.broadcast_to(np.linspace(0, 1, base.shape[1])[None, :, None], base.shape)\n    variables = [np.ones_like(base), horizon,\n                 np.clip(np.abs(anchor - base) / scale, 0, 2),\n                 np.clip(np.abs(recent - base) / scale, 0, 2),\n                 np.broadcast_to(np.clip(np.std(history, axis=1)[:, None, :] / scale, 0, 2), base.shape),\n                 np.clip(np.abs(correction) / 20, 0, 3),\n                 np.clip(np.sign(correction) * (anchor - base) / scale, -2, 2)]\n    return np.stack(variables, axis=-1).reshape(-1, len(variables))\n\n\ndef _amplitude_fit(features, target, tree, network, gate):\n    base = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float64)\n    correction = tree + _weight(gate, features, tree, network) * (network - tree) - base\n    valid = (np.isfinite(target) & (target > 0)).reshape(-1)\n    x = _amplitude_design(features, correction)[valid]\n    center = x.mean(axis=0)\n    center[0] = 0\n    scale = np.maximum(x.std(axis=0), 0.1)\n    scale[0] = 1\n    x = np.clip((x - center) / scale, -4, 4)\n    residual = (base - target).reshape(-1)[valid]\n    correction = correction.reshape(-1)[valid]\n    def objective(coef):\n        activation = np.tanh(x @ coef)\n        error = residual + (1 + 0.5 * activation) * correction\n        smooth = np.sqrt(error * error + 4)\n        derivative = error / smooth * correction * 0.5 * (1 - activation * activation)\n        return (np.mean(smooth) / 20 + 0.02 * np.dot(coef, coef) / 2,\n                x.T @ derivative / (len(x) * 20) + 0.02 * coef)\n    result = minimize(objective, np.zeros(x.shape[1]), jac=True, method='L-BFGS-B',\n                      options={'maxiter': 60, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    return {'coef': result.x.astype(np.float32), 'center': center.astype(np.float32),\n            'scale': scale.astype(np.float32)}\n\n\ndef _blend(gate, features, tree, network, amplitude=None):\n    blend = tree + _weight(gate, features, tree, network) * (network - tree)\n    if amplitude is not None:\n        base = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float64)\n        correction = blend - base\n        x = _amplitude_design(features, correction)\n        x = np.clip((x - amplitude['center']) / amplitude['scale'], -4, 4)\n        factor = (1 + 0.5 * np.tanh(x @ amplitude['coef'])).reshape(base.shape)\n        blend = np.maximum(base + factor * correction, 0)\n    return blend\n\n\ndef fit(features, targets, seed, auxiliary_mode=None, site_head=False, average=False,\n        gate_mode='standard', amplitude=False):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        y = np.asarray(targets['target'] if isinstance(targets, dict) else targets)\n        index = np.arange(len(y))\n        tree_oof, network_oof = np.empty_like(y), np.empty_like(y)\n        for held in np.array_split(index, 3):\n            train = np.setdiff1d(index, held)\n            train_features = {k: v[train] for k, v in features.items()}\n            test_features = {k: v[held] for k, v in features.items()}\n            fold = blended_calibration.fit(train_features, y[train], seed,\n                                           site_head=site_head, average=average)\n            tree_oof[held] = horizon_calibration.predict(fold['tree'], test_features)\n            network_oof[held] = neural_calibration.predict(fold['network'], test_features)\n        gate = _gate_fit(features, y, tree_oof, network_oof, mode=gate_mode)\n        state = blended_calibration.fit(features, y, seed, site_head=site_head, average=average)\n        state['gate'] = gate\n        if amplitude:\n            state['amplitude'] = _amplitude_fit(features, y, tree_oof, network_oof, gate)\n        if auxiliary_mode is not None:\n            state['aux_network'] = neural_calibration.fit(\n                features, y, seed, graph=state['tree']['pooled']['graph'], mode=auxiliary_mode)\n        return state\n\n\ndef predict(state, features):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        tree = horizon_calibration.predict(state['tree'], features)\n        network = neural_calibration.predict(state['network'], features)\n        if 'aux_network' in state:\n            network = (network + neural_calibration.predict(state['aux_network'], features)) / 2\n        return _blend(state['gate'], features, tree, network,\n                      state.get('amplitude')).astype(np.float32)\n\n--- neural_calibration.py ---\n\"\"\"Small NumPy residual network trained with a smooth absolute-error objective.\"\"\"\nimport time\nimport numpy as np\nfrom threadpoolctl import threadpool_limits\nimport spatial_calibration\n\n\ndef _features(features, graph, mode='summary'):\n    raw = spatial_calibration._features(features, graph)\n    node = raw[:, 14].astype(np.int64)\n    clock = np.asarray(features['clock']).reshape(-1)\n    periodic = [np.sin(2 * np.pi * clock), np.cos(2 * np.pi * clock),\n                np.sin(4 * np.pi * clock), np.cos(4 * np.pi * clock)]\n    columns = [np.delete(raw, 14, axis=1)] + periodic\n    if mode in ('history', 'relative'):\n        base = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float32)\n        history = np.asarray(features['history'], dtype=np.float32)\n        recent = np.mean(history[:, -3:, :], axis=1)[:, None, :]\n        # The shared network can learn a temporal filter rather than relying\n        # only on fixed three/six-step averages and one trend statistic.\n        columns += [np.broadcast_to(history[:, j:j+1, :] - recent, base.shape).reshape(-1)\n                    for j in range(history.shape[1])]\n        columns += [(base[:, :1, :] - base).reshape(-1),\n                    (base[:, -1:, :] - base).reshape(-1)]\n        if mode == 'relative':\n            anchor = np.asarray(features['anchor'], dtype=np.float32)\n            scale = graph['scale']\n            columns += [np.broadcast_to(scale, base.shape).reshape(-1),\n                        (base / scale).reshape(-1),\n                        ((anchor - base) / scale).reshape(-1),\n                        ((recent - base) / scale).reshape(-1)]\n    return np.column_stack(columns), node\n\n\ndef _head_features(features, mode=True):\n    shape = features['base'].shape\n    clock = np.asarray(features['clock'], dtype=np.float32).reshape(-1)\n    horizon = np.broadcast_to(np.linspace(-1, 1, shape[1])[None, :, None], shape).reshape(-1)\n    if mode == 'trend':\n        return np.column_stack([np.ones_like(clock), horizon]).astype(np.float32)\n    columns = [np.ones_like(clock), horizon,\n               np.sin(2 * np.pi * clock), np.cos(2 * np.pi * clock),\n               np.sin(4 * np.pi * clock), np.cos(4 * np.pi * clock)]\n    if mode == 'innovation':\n        base = np.asarray(features['base'], dtype=np.float32)\n        anchor = np.asarray(features['anchor'], dtype=np.float32)\n        history = np.asarray(features['history'], dtype=np.float32)\n        scale = np.maximum(np.mean(history, axis=1)[:, None, :], 30)\n        recent = np.mean(history[:, -3:, :], axis=1)[:, None, :]\n        last = history[:, -1:, :]\n        columns.extend([np.clip((anchor - base) / scale, -1.5, 1.5).reshape(-1),\n                        np.clip((recent - base) / scale, -1.5, 1.5).reshape(-1),\n                        np.broadcast_to(np.clip((last - recent) / scale, -1, 1), shape).reshape(-1)])\n    return np.column_stack(columns).astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef _forward(x, node, params, head_x=None):\n    xx = np.column_stack([x, params['embedding'][node]])\n    h1 = np.tanh(xx @ params['w1'] + params['b1'])\n    h2 = np.tanh(h1 @ params['w2'] + params['b2'])\n    output = (h2 @ params['w3'] + x @ params['w0'] + params['b3']).reshape(-1)\n    if 'site_head' in params:\n        output += np.sum(head_x * params['site_head'][node], axis=1)\n    return output, (xx, h1, h2)\n\n\ndef fit(features, targets, seed, epochs=100, graph=None, mode='summary', site_head=False, average=False,\n        graph_strength=0.005, embedding_strength=0):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        start = time.monotonic()\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        if graph is None:\n            graph = spatial_calibration._neighborhood(features)\n        x, node = _features(features, graph, mode)\n        y = np.asarray(targets['target'] if isinstance(targets, dict) else targets)\n        valid = (np.isfinite(y) & (y > 0)).reshape(-1)\n        residual = (y - np.asarray(features['base'])).reshape(-1)[valid] / 20\n        x, node = x[valid], node[valid]\n        head_x = _head_features(features, site_head)[valid] if site_head else None\n        laplacian = None\n        if site_head in ('graph', 'innovation') or embedding_strength:\n            adjacency = np.zeros((features['base'].shape[-1], features['base'].shape[-1]), dtype=np.float32)\n            np.put_along_axis(adjacency, graph['neighbors'], graph['weights'], axis=1)\n            adjacency = (adjacency + adjacency.T) / 2\n            laplacian = np.diag(adjacency.sum(axis=1)) - adjacency\n        center = np.mean(x, axis=0)\n        scale = np.maximum(np.std(x, axis=0), 0.01)\n        x = np.clip((x - center) / scale, -8, 8).astype(np.float32)\n        dim = x.shape[1] + 6\n        params = {'embedding': (rng.normal(size=(features['base'].shape[-1], 6)) * 0.05).astype(np.float32),\n                  'w1': (rng.normal(size=(dim, 48)) / np.sqrt(dim)).astype(np.float32),\n                  'b1': np.zeros(48, dtype=np.float32),\n                  'w2': (rng.normal(size=(48, 24)) / np.sqrt(48)).astype(np.float32),\n                  'b2': np.zeros(24, dtype=np.float32),\n                  'w0': np.zeros((x.shape[1], 1), dtype=np.float32),\n                  'w3': np.zeros((24, 1), dtype=np.float32),\n                  'b3': np.array([np.median(residual)], dtype=np.float32)}\n        if site_head:\n            params['site_head'] = np.zeros((features['base'].shape[-1], head_x.shape[1]), dtype=np.float32)\n        first = {k: np.zeros_like(v) for k, v in params.items()}\n        second = {k: np.zeros_like(v) for k, v in params.items()}\n        average_params = {k: np.zeros_like(v) for k, v in params.items()} if average else None\n        average_count = 0\n        step = 0\n        for epoch in range(epochs):\n            order = rng.permutation(x.shape[0])\n            rate = 0.003 * (0.35 + 0.65 * (1 - epoch / epochs))\n            for offset in range(0, len(order), 4096):\n                index = order[offset:offset + 4096]\n                output, (xx, h1, h2) = _forward(x[index], node[index], params,\n                                             head_x[index] if site_head else None)\n                error = output - residual[index]\n                dout = (error / np.sqrt(error * error + 0.01) / len(index))[:, None]\n                gradients = {'w0': x[index].T @ dout, 'w3': h2.T @ dout, 'b3': dout.sum(axis=0)}\n                dh2 = (dout @ params['w3'].T) * (1 - h2 * h2)\n                gradients.update(w2=h1.T @ dh2, b2=dh2.sum(axis=0))\n                dh1 = (dh2 @ params['w2'].T) * (1 - h1 * h1)\n                gradients.update(w1=xx.T @ dh1, b1=dh1.sum(axis=0))\n                dembed = (dh1 @ params['w1'].T)[:, -6:]\n                gradients['embedding'] = np.zeros_like(params['embedding'])\n                np.add.at(gradients['embedding'], node[index], dembed)\n                if site_head:\n                    gradients['site_head'] = np.zeros_like(params['site_head'])\n                    np.add.at(gradients['site_head'], node[index], head_x[index] * dout)\n                step += 1\n                for key, gradient in gradients.items():\n                    if key == 'site_head':\n                        gradient = gradient + params[key] * 0.0005\n                        if laplacian is not None:\n                            gradient[:, 2:] += graph_strength * (laplacian @ params[key][:, 2:])\n                    elif key.startswith('w') or key == 'embedding':\n                        gradient = gradient + params[key] * 0.0002\n                        if key == 'embedding' and embedding_strength:\n                            gradient += embedding_strength * (laplacian @ params[key])\n                    first[key] = 0.9 * first[key] + 0.1 * gradient\n                    second[key] = 0.999 * second[key] + 0.001 * gradient * gradient\n                    corrected = first[key] / (1 - 0.9 ** step)\n                    variance = second[key] / (1 - 0.999 ** step)\n                    params[key] -= rate * corrected / (np.sqrt(variance) + 1e-7)\n            if average and epoch >= 3 * epochs // 4:\n                for key in params:\n                    average_params[key] += params[key]\n                average_count += 1\n            if time.monotonic() - start > 150:\n                break\n        state = {'graph': graph, 'center': center, 'scale': scale, 'params': params, 'mode': mode,\n                 'epochs': epoch + 1, 'fit_seconds': time.monotonic() - start, 'head_mode': site_head}\n        if average_count:\n            state['last_params'] = params\n            state['params'] = {key: value / average_count for key, value in average_params.items()}\n        return state\n\n\ndef predict(state, features):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        x, node = _features(features, state['graph'], state.get('mode', 'summary'))\n        x = np.clip((x - state['center']) / state['scale'], -8, 8).astype(np.float32)\n        head_x = _head_features(features, state.get('head_mode', True)) if 'site_head' in state['params'] else None\n        residual = np.empty(x.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n        for offset in range(0, len(x), 8192):\n            end = offset + 8192\n            residual[offset:end] = _forward(x[offset:end], node[offset:end], state['params'],\n                                          head_x[offset:end] if head_x is not None else None)[0] * 20\n        return np.maximum(np.asarray(features['base']) + residual.reshape(features['base'].shape), 0).astype(np.float32)\n\n--- stacked_calibration.py ---\n\"\"\"Cross-fitted tree forecasts with a smooth residual correction network.\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom threadpoolctl import threadpool_limits\nimport horizon_calibration\nimport neural_calibration\n\n\ndef _with_base(features, base):\n    return {**features, 'base': base}\n\n\ndef fit(features, targets, seed):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        y = np.asarray(targets['target'] if isinstance(targets, dict) else targets)\n        out_of_fold = np.zeros_like(y)\n        index = np.arange(len(y))\n        for held in np.array_split(index, 3):\n            train = np.setdiff1d(index, held)\n            fold = horizon_calibration.fit({k: v[train] for k, v in features.items()}, y[train], seed, groups=2)\n            out_of_fold[held] = horizon_calibration.predict(fold, {k: v[held] for k, v in features.items()})\n        network = neural_calibration.fit(_with_base(features, out_of_fold), y, seed)\n        tree = horizon_calibration.fit(features, y, seed, groups=2)\n        return {'tree': tree, 'network': network, 'correction_weight': 0.25}\n\n\ndef predict(state, features):\n    with threadpool_limits(limits=2):\n        tree = horizon_calibration.predict(state['tree'], features)\n        corrected = neural_calibration.predict(state['network'], _with_base(features, tree))\n        weight = state['correction_weight']\n        return (tree * (1 - weight) + corrected * weight).astype(np.float32)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
